    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nWhen opening netrw explorer with a single buffer in two windows, :Explore will collapse the split. So there now is only one window with netrw open.\n\nI have checked and this behaviour is different from vim version 8.2.\n\nI've looked around and think the issue might be in s:NetrwBufRename, adding `bufwinid(oldbufnr) == -1` to the check before calling bwipe solves it on my end.\n\nI also confirmed that oldbufnr was still displayed in another window when bwipe! was called. Adding the condition prevents that buffer from being wiped while it's displayed.\n\nBut, I haven't looked too much at the code so I am not sure this is a good fix.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nnvim --clean\n:edit foo.txt\n:split\n:Explore\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nnetrw is opened in the active window, just like how it would be in case of\nnvim --clean\n:split\n:Explore\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nNVIM v0.13.0-dev-1959+g61e71ccf8a\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nno, vim 8.2\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nwindows 11\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nWindows Terminal 1.24.12741.0\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nTERM: Not set (Windows Terminal / PowerShell)\n\n### Installation\n\nbuild from repo, but checked nightly from .zip",
